1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,170
I know what that madam said
was pretty accurate,

3
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:07,030
but I find it scary.

4
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,810
I know a psychic who's really good.

5
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:10,770
I can introduce him to you.

6
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:12,140
Every time I have
a relationship problem...

7
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:13,500
Forget it.

8
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:16,140
It's okay. I want to go home.

9
00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:17,860
I'll go with you.

10
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:19,490
It's fine.

11
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,160
Don't you have to go back to work?

12
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:25,510
I'm not feeling well.
Help me apply for sick leave.

13
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,290
And apologize to Ms. Chang-fen.

14
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:32,030
Actually, there's nothing urgent at work.

15
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:34,840
It's okay. You should go.

16
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:37,440
I'm okay.

17
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:41,750
If you want to go see the fortune-teller,

18
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,020
call me.

19
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:44,210
Okay.

20
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:48,300
That fortune-teller was really good.

21
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:09,160
[Cross the street at the traffic light.]

22
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:12,280
[Walk 20 steps to the west.]

23
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:15,190
[You'll come to a street lamp.]

24
00:01:30,539 --> 00:01:34,060
[Circle the lamp three times
with your eyes closed.]

25
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:37,140
[Then take 20 steps forward.]

26
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,579
[You'll find]

27
00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:38,700
[the path that you thought was a dead end]

28
00:02:38,829 --> 00:02:40,370
[is not what you had imagined.]

29
00:03:00,610 --> 00:03:01,880
What are you doing?

30
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:06,020
What are you doing here?

31
00:03:09,050 --> 00:03:10,330
What are you doing here?

32
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,230
I'm worried about you two.

33
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,870
Didn't you wish for me to die?

34
00:03:18,950 --> 00:03:21,370
Then why are you here to save me

35
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:22,740
and won't let me die?

36
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:28,720
If I'm not mistaken, it's because

37
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:31,760
I can't die at this time, right?

38
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,260
Little girl, you're very clever.

39
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:35,010
That small head of yours...

40
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:36,820
Shut up.

41
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:39,370
Okay, I'll shut up.

42
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,180
So you saved me

43
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,650
because I can't die yet.

44
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:47,290
I need to die

45
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,490
the way you said I would.

46
00:03:49,579 --> 00:03:52,610
On that rainy night next Monday.

47
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,940
That's the only way to fulfill

48
00:03:55,030 --> 00:03:57,500
Kakarayan's arrangement.

49
00:03:58,510 --> 00:04:02,640
If I died now...

50
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:06,910
That would be a problem.

51
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,980
Right, a big problem.

52
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,050
So even if you're gods,

53
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:13,030
there's nothing you can do to me.

54
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,649
If I didn't know when I'd die,

55
00:04:17,730 --> 00:04:20,329
I wouldn't be able to change my fate.

56
00:04:20,899 --> 00:04:22,050
But now,

57
00:04:24,110 --> 00:04:25,830
I'll do whatever it takes

58
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,680
to avoid that intersection

59
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,190
next Monday night.

60
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,400
There's nothing you can do to me.

61
00:04:34,590 --> 00:04:36,960
Instead, you will be

62
00:04:38,590 --> 00:04:41,760
in a whole load of trouble.

63
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,430
Are you having fun?

64
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,450
Is this fun?

65
00:04:56,890 --> 00:04:58,610
Does anyone have
next week's tour schedules?

66
00:04:58,700 --> 00:04:59,530
Do you have it?

67
00:04:59,659 --> 00:05:00,410
Yes.

68
00:05:02,790 --> 00:05:03,490
Here you go.

69
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:05,650
Thank you.

70
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:09,870
It's this day.

71
00:05:11,810 --> 00:05:13,080
Didn't you say you wanted to rest at home?

72
00:05:13,170 --> 00:05:13,960
Why are you here?

73
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,420
There's a good saying.

74
00:05:15,990 --> 00:05:19,200
The only person you can trust is yourself.

75
00:05:20,390 --> 00:05:21,440
I might as well do it myself.

76
00:05:26,150 --> 00:05:27,520
Didn't I tell you?

77
00:05:27,690 --> 00:05:29,360
Don't be superstitious.

78
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,530
Superstitions shouldn't be allowed.

79
00:05:32,930 --> 00:05:33,680
They're no good.

80
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:35,040
Give me that.

81
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:37,060
Did you hear what she just said?

82
00:05:41,370 --> 00:05:42,780
Ms. Chang-fen.

83
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:45,470
Aren't you...

84
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,490
I know Yi-han asked for a day off for me.

85
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:50,350
But I came here to tell you something.

86
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:51,710
For the immediate future,

87
00:05:51,850 --> 00:05:53,210
I want to be a part of all the tours

88
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:54,970
that are outside of Taipei.

89
00:05:56,110 --> 00:05:56,950
All of them?

90
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:57,650
Yes, all of them.

91
00:05:58,450 --> 00:05:59,330
No.

92
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,690
I've already planned
for tomorrow morning's Taitung...

93
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:03,590
Ms. Chang-fen,
I'm telling you loud and clear.

94
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:05,310
As long as the tour is away from Taipei,

95
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:08,700
I'm willing to do
whatever it takes to be in it.

96
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,280
You're very enthusiastic.

97
00:06:12,350 --> 00:06:13,270
Okay.

98
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:16,000
It's because you're number one, the ace.

99
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,200
The fourth hitter.

100
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,020
Thank you, Ms. Chang-fen.

101
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:21,810
You're welcome.

102
00:06:26,470 --> 00:06:29,330
Ma'am, you're really good.

103
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:30,870
I didn't say anything,

104
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:33,070
but you knew everything.

105
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:37,080
It's your life that's telling me this.

106
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:38,659
Trust me.

107
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:42,220
It won't be long
before he comes back for you.

108
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:44,070
If he doesn't,

109
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,650
you can always come back to me.

110
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:53,880
Thank you, ma'am.

111
00:07:01,450 --> 00:07:03,170
What are you up to?

112
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:09,990
What am I up to?

113
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:11,790
Don't you think

114
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:14,300
it's weird coming from you?

115
00:07:14,430 --> 00:07:15,840
As the all-knowing messenger

116
00:07:15,930 --> 00:07:17,470
that can see the Reflection of Time,

117
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:19,010
I think you would know the answer.

118
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,700
Or could it be that everything
that's happening right now

119
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:24,110
is different from what you saw

120
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,210
in the Reflection of Time,

121
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:26,310
so even you don't know

122
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,420
what will happen next?

123
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:31,060
Do you want to know?

124
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:33,260
I can divine it for you.

125
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:21,220
[August 10th, 2009.]

126
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:25,270
[Today, I received]

127
00:08:25,350 --> 00:08:27,470
[my first ever paycheck.]

128
00:08:28,790 --> 00:08:31,510
[I bought a Polaroid camera.]

129
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:32,659
Let's take a photo.

130
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:34,950
[The first photo taken...]

131
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,220
Hurry up.

132
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:38,159
[was of me and him of course.]

133
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:43,390
One, two, three.

134
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:52,990
It's no use.

135
00:08:53,690 --> 00:08:54,700
You can't take my picture.

136
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:56,900
Why not?

137
00:08:57,960 --> 00:08:59,940
Because I won't appear in the photo.

138
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:03,190
You can only see me

139
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:04,600
when I want you to see me.

140
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:06,400
You should've said so earlier.

141
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:08,740
So I wasted this film?

142
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,050
I've got your shot.

143
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:18,720
No way.

144
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:19,650
It's true.

145
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:20,530
There's no way.

146
00:09:22,070 --> 00:09:23,610
It's true.

147
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:24,710
That's impossible. Let me see.

148
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:32,060
Let me see.

149
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:42,040
Where?

150
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:46,000
Have you forgotten what you told me?

151
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:49,040
That I'm the only one who can see you

152
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,890
and feel your presence in this world.

153
00:09:52,730 --> 00:09:54,540
That's why even if others think

154
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:56,520
that I'm the only one in this photo,

155
00:09:57,350 --> 00:09:58,500
I know

156
00:10:00,170 --> 00:10:01,490
that you're here next to me.

157
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:09,410
Let's waste another negative.

158
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:25,210
Is he really...

159
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:29,690
[But aren't you my guardian angel?]

160
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:32,860
[Then why are you trying to kill me?]

161
00:10:32,950 --> 00:10:34,840
That's not important.

162
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,540
You'll forget everything soon.

163
00:10:46,810 --> 00:10:49,140
[April 6th, 2016.]

164
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,260
[It rained all day today.]

165
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:55,520
[When I walked back to the office
with the umbrella,]

166
00:10:55,650 --> 00:10:57,810
[I couldn't help but think]

167
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,180
[that this was]

168
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:03,920
[the scenery he usually saw.]

169
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:15,800
[Shanfeng Tours]

170
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:22,530
♫ I don't remember where it was ♫

171
00:11:22,930 --> 00:11:28,030
♫ That I saw those pair of eyes ♫

172
00:11:28,390 --> 00:11:32,870
♫ In the dream where it rained so hard ♫

173
00:11:33,530 --> 00:11:35,730
♫ I'm in your arms ♫

174
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:44,490
♫ I can't tell which memories ♫

175
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:49,900
♫ Should be forgotten or remembered ♫

176
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:54,780
♫ Don't want it to just be a game ♫

177
00:11:55,310 --> 00:11:58,080
♫ I can't help it ♫

178
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:02,570
♫ So many things I wish to tell you ♫

179
00:12:02,660 --> 00:12:05,210
♫ I don't want to keep it inside ♫

180
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:06,140
This is for you.

181
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,680
I made it myself.

182
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,440
What is this?

183
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:16,300
My Japanese language teacher said

184
00:12:16,430 --> 00:12:18,940
that if I want it to be sunny every day,

185
00:12:19,290 --> 00:12:20,700
I can draw a fair-weather doll

186
00:12:20,830 --> 00:12:22,240
with a smiling face

187
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:23,520
and hang it on the window.

188
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,340
Is this a fair-weather doll?

189
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:31,790
No.

190
00:12:35,170 --> 00:12:36,980
I made one bad-weather doll

191
00:12:37,110 --> 00:12:39,130
with a crying face

192
00:12:39,350 --> 00:12:40,630
to hang on the window.

193
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:43,840
I pray that it will rain every day.

194
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:48,900
Who wants it to rain every day?

195
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,070
There is someone.

196
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,450
Me.

197
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:56,870
Why do you want it to rain every day?

198
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:02,890
If it rains every day,

199
00:13:03,910 --> 00:13:05,140
then...

200
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:07,820
I'll be able

201
00:13:09,270 --> 00:13:12,350
to see you all the time.

202
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:21,590
[Why does he seem so gentle]

203
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:25,200
[from what I can remember?]

204
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:31,320
♫ I will know the kindness
behind your poker face ♫

205
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:35,500
♫ Where will we go to enjoy the breeze? ♫

206
00:13:35,630 --> 00:13:38,050
♫ Until the next sunset ♫

207
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:42,140
♫ Today, when you said you love me ♫

208
00:13:42,230 --> 00:13:45,220
♫ Won't leave, won't let go ♫

209
00:13:45,310 --> 00:13:47,680
♫ Until the world disappears ♫

210
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:50,320
♫ Let the tears ♫

211
00:13:50,410 --> 00:13:53,180
♫ Follow the wind ♫

212
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:56,840
♫ And seal the promise ♫

213
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,410
Share the blessings.

214
00:14:50,290 --> 00:14:50,910
Hurry up.

215
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:54,120
I think it's for us.

216
00:14:54,210 --> 00:14:55,040
Snacks.

217
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:55,880
Thank you.

218
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:56,980
It's delicious.

219
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,140
What should I do?

220
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:00,720
Say something.

221
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:06,310
Hello, I'm Wu Yi-han.

222
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,160
I look forward to our time together.

223
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,360
I'll keep it in my heart.

224
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,460
Click!

225
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,210
What now?

226
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,430
-Think of a story I used to tell.
-What are we doing in the rain like this?

227
00:15:21,970 --> 00:15:24,350
Yes, what is this?

228
00:15:24,430 --> 00:15:25,530
Attention.

229
00:15:26,410 --> 00:15:29,010
Let me tell you guys a story. Okay?

230
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:29,540
Okay.

231
00:15:31,910 --> 00:15:36,090
Once upon a time,
a pair of siblings lived by themselves

232
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:38,870
in poverty.

233
00:15:39,390 --> 00:15:40,450
One year...

234
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:44,010
One year...

235
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,550
One year?

236
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,490
What is she saying? I think she forgot.

237
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:49,730
Last time, you said
there was a brother and sister.

238
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,540
There was a poor father or something.

239
00:15:51,670 --> 00:15:54,840
One year, their tribe was suffering
from a serious drought.

240
00:15:54,930 --> 00:15:56,030
Right.

241
00:15:56,730 --> 00:16:00,160
One year, there was a drought.

242
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:03,900
There was a serious water shortage
in the tribe.

243
00:16:03,990 --> 00:16:06,580
Only the siblings' house had water,

244
00:16:07,330 --> 00:16:09,440
[It has been a while
since I visited Grandma.]

245
00:16:10,410 --> 00:16:11,690
[This place hasn't changed.]

246
00:16:19,430 --> 00:16:22,560
[I wonder if Grandma is here.]

247
00:16:41,830 --> 00:16:42,750
That's all.

248
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:43,280
The end.

249
00:16:46,230 --> 00:16:47,190
Tien-ti.

250
00:16:47,330 --> 00:16:49,530
How did you have time
to prepare these fairy tales?

251
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:50,930
You even remember every little detail.

252
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:53,840
My grandma told me these stories.

253
00:16:54,940 --> 00:16:55,640
Your grandma?

254
00:16:57,490 --> 00:16:59,430
I haven't seen her in a while.

255
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:02,370
I wonder how she's doing.

256
00:17:02,510 --> 00:17:04,490
Pu, take a photo for us.

257
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:06,770
Together.

258
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:07,829
Keep it in my heart.

259
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:08,800
Okay.

260
00:17:09,150 --> 00:17:10,470
One, two, three.

261
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:13,460
Keep it in my heart.

262
00:17:13,550 --> 00:17:14,390
Okay.

263
00:17:26,569 --> 00:17:27,720
Banai.

264
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:37,570
Banai, don't be sad.

265
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,290
Cariwciw.

266
00:17:40,650 --> 00:17:44,220
I'm not sad. I'm lonely.

267
00:17:46,990 --> 00:17:49,850
I know, you must think

268
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,210
that after she left,

269
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:52,050
you are this tribe's

270
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:53,630
last Sikawasay or medium.

271
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:56,230
That's why you feel lonely, right?

272
00:18:01,770 --> 00:18:04,370
No matter what, you'll always have me.

273
00:18:05,070 --> 00:18:06,300
I'll be right next to you.

274
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:12,770
Banai, stop it with the long face.

275
00:18:13,250 --> 00:18:14,710
I'm your guardian angel.

276
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:17,210
I'll be there when you need me.

277
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:19,990
We're inseparable.

278
00:18:29,490 --> 00:18:30,810
I'm warning you.

279
00:18:31,030 --> 00:18:32,970
Whatever brings your here today,

280
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:35,170
Banai is already in a bad mood.

281
00:18:35,430 --> 00:18:37,060
Stop using the name of Kakarayan

282
00:18:37,150 --> 00:18:39,040
to make her do something
that will upset her.

283
00:18:41,330 --> 00:18:43,220
I'm not here for her.

284
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:47,310
It's you.

285
00:19:00,730 --> 00:19:01,610
What's wrong?

286
00:19:02,750 --> 00:19:03,900
What did he say to you?

287
00:19:19,910 --> 00:19:21,360
[Why are you doing this?]

288
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:27,000
Is this really Kakarayan's arrangement?

289
00:19:27,830 --> 00:19:29,150
Answer me!

290
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:41,600
What is it?

291
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:43,630
All data have been compiled.

292
00:19:43,710 --> 00:19:45,210
We can leave anytime now.

293
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:46,570
Okay, good.

294
00:19:49,830 --> 00:19:51,020
Is there any other problem?

295
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:54,710
We're evacuating
all the Kawas next Monday.

296
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:56,080
I worry that 'Orad

297
00:19:56,170 --> 00:19:57,350
won't be able to take care

298
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:59,250
of that girl called Hsieh Tien-ti in time.

299
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:01,180
That's his problem, not ours.

300
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:03,120
But I heard she has fled to Taitung.

301
00:20:03,290 --> 00:20:04,660
If she doesn't return to Taipei

302
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:06,070
and die in that rain,

303
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:07,300
that will disrupt Kakarayan's plan.

304
00:20:07,430 --> 00:20:08,490
I told you.

305
00:20:10,950 --> 00:20:12,270
It's none of our business.

306
00:20:14,690 --> 00:20:15,970
I know it's not our business.

307
00:20:16,410 --> 00:20:17,460
But I just can't stand it

308
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:18,600
when something
that could be done perfectly

309
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:20,010
ends up having flaws.

310
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:24,100
She's trying to change her fate,

311
00:20:24,190 --> 00:20:25,340
but she doesn't realize

312
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:26,790
that whatever she tries to do

313
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:27,980
will still bring her back

314
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,520
to Kakarayan's plan.

315
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,300
In His plan,

316
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:34,400
the Hsieh Tien-ti now

317
00:20:34,490 --> 00:20:36,380
is meant to be in Taitung,

318
00:20:38,450 --> 00:20:39,940
at her current location,

319
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:42,190
doing what she's doing.

320
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:56,440
This shop

321
00:20:56,580 --> 00:21:01,110
is the most famous
local aboriginal restaurant.

322
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,690
That's great.

323
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:03,970
What is this?

324
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:05,370
These are fried crown daisies.

325
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:06,780
Fried crown daisy.

326
00:21:08,010 --> 00:21:09,070
Then what is this?

327
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:11,360
-Well...
-I'm curious.

328
00:21:13,210 --> 00:21:14,570
I don't think she knows.

329
00:21:15,890 --> 00:21:18,350
Enjoy the food.

330
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:21,260
I'll enjoy this meal.

331
00:21:21,350 --> 00:21:22,620
How would I know what that is?

332
00:21:22,710 --> 00:21:24,820
You did well.

333
00:21:25,390 --> 00:21:27,370
Right, Do Myeong-jun doesn't eat pork.

334
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:29,350
You didn't order a pork dish, did you?

335
00:21:29,790 --> 00:21:31,510
Of course not. Who am I?

336
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:33,580
I remember everything.

337
00:21:33,670 --> 00:21:34,720
Smart girl.

338
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:36,880
Also, there was a delay
due to the rain today.

339
00:21:37,010 --> 00:21:39,690
Did you tell the hotel
that we're going to be late?

340
00:21:46,030 --> 00:21:47,610
You go ahead. I'll make a call.

341
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:48,890
I'll leave it to you.

342
00:22:00,330 --> 00:22:01,030
Hello.

343
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:03,190
I'm Hsieh Tien-ti from Shanfeng Tours.

344
00:22:03,450 --> 00:22:04,330
Yes.

345
00:22:05,170 --> 00:22:06,620
We're checking in a little late today.

346
00:22:06,710 --> 00:22:08,560
Is 9:30 p.m. okay?

347
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:13,480
Okay, thank you.

348
00:22:13,570 --> 00:22:14,720
Okay, bye.

349
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,240
Grandma?

350
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,320
Grandma!

351
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:04,560
Grandma.

352
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:14,730
Grandma.

353
00:23:23,530 --> 00:23:24,630
Grandma.

354
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:28,590
I told you this isn't your house.

355
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:29,860
Go home.

356
00:24:16,110 --> 00:24:18,610
Cry if you want to.

357
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:27,280
♫ As love changes day by day ♫

358
00:24:27,770 --> 00:24:30,930
♫ Just pretend it doesn't matter ♫

359
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:34,760
♫ The end of the world ♫

360
00:24:36,170 --> 00:24:42,020
♫ Maybe I can't compromise anymore ♫

361
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:49,370
♫ It hurts so bad, so bad ♫

362
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:52,490
♫ Tears fall like the rain ♫

363
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:54,740
You won't feel so sad anymore.

364
00:24:55,570 --> 00:24:58,700
You won't remember coming here
to see your grandma today.

365
00:24:59,750 --> 00:25:01,160
You won't remember

366
00:25:01,250 --> 00:25:02,830
the hurtful words

367
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:04,550
that your grandma said.

368
00:25:04,810 --> 00:25:09,480
[Meihe Community]

369
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:06,660
You came here

370
00:25:06,790 --> 00:25:09,210
because you wanted to see the sea.

371
00:25:10,180 --> 00:25:11,850
Then you'll go back to Taipei

372
00:25:12,730 --> 00:25:14,140
for good.

373
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:17,130
Because this place

374
00:25:17,790 --> 00:25:20,030
no longer has anyone worth remembering.

375
00:26:37,650 --> 00:26:38,920
[Don't be so angry.]

376
00:26:38,920 --> 00:27:11,700
[Next episode]

377
00:26:39,010 --> 00:26:40,590
[Whether she dies
by Kakarayan's arrangement]

378
00:26:40,680 --> 00:26:42,000
[or by my hands,]

379
00:26:42,090 --> 00:26:43,010
what's the difference?

380
00:26:43,100 --> 00:26:44,030
[So since the moment]

381
00:26:44,110 --> 00:26:45,790
[you became my guardian angel,]

382
00:26:45,870 --> 00:26:48,250
you've known what would happen?

383
00:26:48,340 --> 00:26:50,320
This is the future of humanity.

384
00:26:50,410 --> 00:26:53,350
[Kakarayan is taking all the Kawas
away from this world.]

385
00:26:53,790 --> 00:26:55,160
[Under the same rain,]

386
00:26:55,250 --> 00:26:57,530
[every person has to go down]

387
00:26:57,620 --> 00:26:59,560
[their own path that He has prepared.]

388
00:26:59,650 --> 00:27:01,540
[When I met you again,]

389
00:27:01,670 --> 00:27:03,610
I finally remembered

390
00:27:03,690 --> 00:27:06,470
[the thing that was so important to me.]

391
00:27:06,550 --> 00:27:07,610
[Guardian angel.]

392
00:27:07,740 --> 00:27:10,650
[Will there be a next life after death?]

393
00:27:13,420 --> 00:27:16,100
[2002, I was very lucky]

394
00:27:29,260 --> 00:27:30,400
Why aren't you in class?

395
00:27:31,060 --> 00:27:32,690
I don't want to go in there.

396
00:27:33,260 --> 00:27:35,720
I don't know any of them.

397
00:27:36,740 --> 00:27:37,920
That's because you just transferred.

398
00:27:38,060 --> 00:27:39,680
You'll make friends soon enough.

399
00:27:40,520 --> 00:27:42,150
I don't want to be friends with them.

400
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:43,690
Those stupid boys.

401
00:27:43,780 --> 00:27:45,230
I don't know who told them.

402
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:48,040
They called me a loser and a jinx.

403
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:50,330
They made fun of me
for not having parents.

404
00:27:50,420 --> 00:27:51,920
Even Grandma doesn't want me.

405
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:53,850
Who said so?

406
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:55,130
I'll teach them a lesson.

407
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:59,530
No, it's okay. They're right.

408
00:28:00,230 --> 00:28:02,080
I don't have a mom or a dad.

409
00:28:02,430 --> 00:28:04,230
Grandma doesn't want me either.

410
00:28:12,510 --> 00:28:14,530
But I know

411
00:28:14,620 --> 00:28:17,430
that I'm not a loser or a jinx.

412
00:28:18,230 --> 00:28:19,240
Because compared to them,

413
00:28:19,330 --> 00:28:21,880
I'm much luckier.

414
00:28:23,110 --> 00:28:23,860
Is that so?

415
00:28:25,790 --> 00:28:27,730
Who in the world is like me?

416
00:28:27,820 --> 00:28:29,580
I have a personal guardian angel.

417
00:28:29,670 --> 00:28:31,510
No matter how bad things get,

418
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:35,780
I have you by my side to protect me.

419
00:28:35,910 --> 00:28:36,840
Doesn't that make me

420
00:28:36,930 --> 00:28:39,520
much luckier than them?

421
00:28:43,610 --> 00:28:44,450
Guardian angel.

422
00:28:44,540 --> 00:28:46,870
You'll always be by my side, right?

423
00:28:58,750 --> 00:28:59,760
It's time for class. Let's go.

424
00:29:01,830 --> 00:29:02,490
Come on.
